# DepositGuard — environment variables reference
# Copy to .env and fill in your values: cp .env.example .env
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SECURITY LEGEND
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#   [SECRET]   NEVER commit. Rotate immediately if leaked.
#              → Store in GCP Secret Manager, Vercel env, or CI secrets.
#
#   [SAFE]     Non-sensitive identifier or config. Can be hardcoded or
#              committed for non-prod, but env injection is always cleaner
#              (a config change won't require a code commit + redeploy).
#
#   [PUBLIC]   Intentionally visible in client-side bundles (NEXT_PUBLIC_
#              prefix). Committing the value is technically fine for public
#              identifiers, but prefer env injection so you can swap values
#              without a code redeploy.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  YOU CAN TECHNICALLY COMMIT / HARDCODE THESE — but it's not recommended
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Variable                              Why it's "safe"
#  ──────────────────────────────────    ───────────────────────────────────────
#  GCP_PROJECT_ID                        Public project identifier — visible in
#                                        GCP console URLs, not a credential.
#
#  GCP_LOCATION                          A region string (e.g. us-central1).
#                                        Contains no secrets.
#
#  FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET               Bucket name is publicly derivable from
#                                        the project ID. Not a credential.
#
#  SOLANA_RPC_URL                        Points to a public RPC endpoint.
#                                        devnet default is safe; prod Helius/
#                                        QuickNode URLs carry no wallet access.
#
#  SOLANA_CLUSTER                        Label string only ("devnet",
#                                        "mainnet-beta"). No access control.
#
#  NEST_CROW_PROGRAM_ID                  On-chain program IDs are public by
#                                        definition — visible to everyone on
#                                        Solscan the moment you deploy.
#
#  APP_BASE_URL                          Your public domain. Already in DNS.
#
#  SENDGRID_FROM_EMAIL                   A verified sender address.
#                                        Not a credential.
#
#  NOTIFY_SERVICE_URL                    Internal service routing. Only
#                                        meaningful inside your VPC/network.
#
#  PORT                                  A port number. No secrets.
#
#  NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVEN_AGENT_PLATFORM_GUIDE
#                                        Sent to every browser by design via
#                                        the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix. Committing
#                                        is fine for public agent IDs.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  NEVER COMMIT THESE — rotate immediately if any are ever exposed
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Variable                  Risk if leaked
#  ────────────────────────  ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  ORACLE_KEYPAIR_BASE58     Full control of the oracle wallet — on-chain funds
#                            and authority signatures can be drained or forged.
#
#  RELAYER_KEYPAIR_BASE58    Same as above for the relayer wallet.
#
#  JWT_SIGNING_SECRET        Anyone with this value can mint valid JWTs and
#                            impersonate any user — complete auth bypass.
#
#  SENDGRID_API_KEY          Can send email as your verified domain, create
#                            spam campaigns, and incur billing charges.
#
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── GCP / Firebase ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SAFE] Your Google Cloud project identifier.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://console.cloud.google.com
#     2. Select your project from the top-left dropdown
#     3. The Project ID appears in the dashboard header (not the display name)
#   OR run: gcloud config get-value project
GCP_PROJECT_ID=

# [SAFE] GCP region where Cloud Run services and Vertex AI are deployed.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     Pick the region closest to your users:
#     https://cloud.google.com/about/locations
#   Common choices: us-central1 | us-east1 | us-west1 | europe-west1
GCP_LOCATION=us-central1

# [SAFE] Firebase Storage bucket name for uploaded files.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://console.firebase.google.com
#     2. Select your project → Build → Storage
#     3. Copy the bucket name shown at the top (e.g. myproject.firebasestorage.app)
#   OR run: firebase use && firebase apps:list
FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=


# ── Solana ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SAFE] Solana JSON-RPC endpoint for on-chain reads/writes.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     Dev/test → use the default below (free, rate-limited)
#     Production → create a free endpoint at:
#       https://www.helius.dev   (recommended)
#       https://www.quicknode.com
#     Copy the HTTPS endpoint URL from your dashboard after creating an app.
SOLANA_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com

# [SAFE] Cluster label used for Solscan explorer links.
#   VALUES: devnet | mainnet-beta
#   Must match the cluster your RPC_URL targets.
SOLANA_CLUSTER=devnet

# [SAFE] Deployed program (smart contract) address.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     Run: anchor build && anchor deploy
#     The program ID is printed after deploy, and also stored in:
#       target/deploy/<program-name>-keypair.json  (public key)
#       Anchor.toml → [programs.devnet] section
#   OR check: https://explorer.solana.com (search your wallet's recent txns)
NEST_CROW_PROGRAM_ID=


# ── Oracle / Relayer keypairs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SECRET] Full oracle keypair encoded as base58 — controls on-chain authority.
#   HOW TO GENERATE (run once, save output securely):
#     node -e "
#       const { Keypair } = require('@solana/web3.js');
#       const bs58 = require('bs58');
#       const kp = Keypair.generate();
#       console.log('Public key :', kp.publicKey.toBase58());
#       console.log('Secret key :', bs58.encode(kp.secretKey));
#     "
#   Store the secret key in Google Cloud Secret Manager:
#     https://console.cloud.google.com/security/secret-manager
#   ⛔  NEVER commit this value — anyone with it can drain the oracle wallet.
ORACLE_KEYPAIR_BASE58=

# [SECRET] Base58-encoded relayer keypair — takes priority over ORACLE_KEYPAIR_BASE58.
#   HOW TO GENERATE: same command as above, use a separate keypair.
#   Why separate? You can rotate the relayer without touching the oracle authority.
#   Store in Google Cloud Secret Manager (separate secret from oracle).
#   ⛔  NEVER commit this value — anyone with it can drain the relayer wallet.
RELAYER_KEYPAIR_BASE58=


# ── Auth / Signing ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SECRET] 32-byte random hex string used to sign and verify JWTs.
#   HOW TO GENERATE:
#     node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
#   ⛔  Rotate immediately if ever exposed — all active sessions will be invalidated.
JWT_SIGNING_SECRET=

# [SAFE] Public base URL of the Next.js app — used to build magic-link email URLs.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     Local dev → http://localhost:3000
#     Production → your custom domain (e.g. https://depositguard.app)
#     Vercel preview → shown in the Vercel dashboard after first deploy
APP_BASE_URL=https://nestcrow.tech


# ── SendGrid ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SECRET] SendGrid API key — authorizes sending transactional email.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://app.sendgrid.com
#     2. Settings → API Keys → Create API Key
#     3. Choose "Full Access" (or "Restricted" with only Mail Send permission)
#     4. Copy the key — it starts with SG. and is shown only once
#   ⛔  Anyone with this key can send email as your verified domain.
SENDGRID_API_KEY=

# [SAFE] Verified sender email address shown as the "From" address.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://app.sendgrid.com
#     2. Settings → Sender Authentication → Verify a Single Sender (or domain)
#     3. Use the email address you verified there
SENDGRID_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@nestcrow.tech


# ── Internal services ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SAFE] URL of the notify Cloud Run service (receives webhook → sends deadline emails).
#   HOW TO GET:
#     Local dev → http://localhost:8080 (default below)
#     Production → shown in Google Cloud Console after deploying the notify service:
#       https://console.cloud.google.com/run
#       Select your service → the URL is displayed at the top of the service page
#   OR run: gcloud run services describe notify --region=$GCP_LOCATION --format='value(status.url)'
NOTIFY_SERVICE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# [SAFE] Port number for local service instances.
#   Change only if 8080 is already in use on your machine.
PORT=8080


# ── Gemini AI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SECRET] Google Gemini Developer API key — used by /api/damage-estimate for
#          multimodal property damage cost estimation via gemini-2.0-flash.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
#     2. Click "Create API key"
#     3. Copy the key (shown once)
#   ⛔  Never commit this value — anyone with it can consume your Gemini quota.
GEMINI_API_KEY=


# ── ElevenLabs ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [SECRET] ElevenLabs API key — authorizes server-side TTS and voice generation calls.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://elevenlabs.io
#     2. Sign in → click your profile → API Keys
#     3. Create a new key and copy it (shown only once)
#   ⛔  Never commit this value — anyone with it can consume your ElevenLabs quota.
#   PRODUCTION: store as GCP Secret Manager secret named "elevenlabs-api-key".
ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=

# [SAFE] ElevenLabs voice ID for the Platform Guide persona ("Eryn").
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://elevenlabs.io → Voice Lab → Voice Design
#     2. Create a calm, professional, gender-neutral voice
#     3. Copy the Voice ID from the voice settings page
#   If unset, defaults to ElevenLabs built-in "Rachel" voice (21m00Tcm4TlvDq8ikWAM).
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_PLATFORM_GUIDE=

# [SAFE] ElevenLabs voice ID for the Dispute Advisor persona.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://elevenlabs.io → Voice Lab → Voice Design
#     2. Create a calm authority voice, slightly slower speaking rate
#     3. Copy the Voice ID from the voice settings page
#   If unset, defaults to ElevenLabs built-in "Adam" voice (pNInz6obpgDQGcFmaJgB).
ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID_DISPUTE_ADVISOR=

# [PUBLIC] ElevenLabs Conversational AI agent ID — sent to every browser via NEXT_PUBLIC_.
#   HOW TO GET:
#     1. Go to https://elevenlabs.io
#     2. Sign in → Conversational AI (left sidebar) → select your agent
#     3. Copy the Agent ID shown at the top of the agent settings page
#   This value is not secret — it is embedded in your client-side JS bundle.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ELEVEN_AGENT_PLATFORM_GUIDE=
